+// resolves to the inherited accessor on `Object.prototype`, so `obj[key] =
+// value` re-parents the object instead of recording an entry, and the entry is
+// silently lost. Defining an own data property shadows that accessor, after
+// which reading, `hasOwnProperty`, `Object.keys` and further assignment all
+// behave like any other key.
